{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> R. Yeshuaah said that the meaning of \"the abomination of Egypt\" is that Moses wrote thus to disgrace idolatry, for he did not say to Pharaoh \"the god of Egypt.\" And he said that their god was in the form of a lamb, for they believed that the constellation of Aries rules over their land, and for this reason they did not eat meat. But if so, why would they not eat beef or the flesh of kids? In my opinion, the people of Egypt in Moses' days held the views of the people of India, who are more than half the world, and all of them are sons of Ham, and they do not eat meat to this day, nor blood, nor fat, nor fish, nor eggs — the principle being anything that comes from a living creature. And they abhor anyone who eats them, and herding is an abomination in their eyes, as it is written, \"for every shepherd of flocks is an abomination to Egypt\" (Genesis 46:34). And to this day they do not permit a person to eat meat in their land, and if one of them comes to a foreign land, he flees from every place where meat is eaten, and he will not eat anything that a meat-eater has touched, and his utensils are impure in their eyes. And so it is written, \"for the Egyptians cannot eat bread with the Hebrews\" (Genesis 43:32). And behold, Joseph when he was in Potiphar's house — they put him in charge of everything except the bread he ate, for he would not touch it because he was a Hebrew. And there is no reason to ask, if so, why did they have livestock — for so it is with the people of India: horses, donkeys, and camels for carrying and riding, cattle for plowing, and sheep for wool. And I will speak further of this in connection with the Pesach of Egypt. Yefet said that the heh is missing from the word \"ולא יסקלונו,\" for the meaning is: will they not stone us? In my opinion, the word הן in הן נזבח has the heh of inquiry, and so it is: would we slaughter the abomination of Egypt before their eyes, and would they not stone us? — like it: הן היתה כזאת (Jeremiah 2:11)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:50.547646731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}